# Tutorial 03 — 2D drafting: shapes, snaps, ortho, trim, offset and fillet.
title: Drawing basics
summary: Lines, polylines, rectangles, circles, snaps, ortho, trim, offset and fillet
---
open new
zoom window -1500,-3000 15500,7500
caption "Shapes" "Rectangles, circles and polylines with arc segments"
type RECTANG 0,0 @6000,4000
type CIRCLE 3000,2000 1200
type PLINE 8000,4000 @3000,0 A @0,2000 L @-3000,0 C
wait 1.5
caption "Object snaps" "OSNAP locks the cursor to endpoints, midpoints and centres"
note "OSNAP is on in the status bar (F3)" at status OSNAP for 3.5
type LINE
move 300,3700
pick 0,4000
type CEN
pick 4200,2000
type MID
pick 6000,1200
enter
wait 1.5
caption "Ortho" "F8 keeps lines horizontal or vertical; type a length to go that far"
click status ORTHO
type LINE 8000,0
move 10500,200
type 3000
move 11100,2200
type 2500
enter
click status ORTHO
wait 1
caption "Fillet" "FILLET rounds the corner between two lines"
type FILLET Radius 800
pick 9500,0
pick 11000,1500
wait 1.5
caption "Trim" "TRIM cuts objects back to the edges they cross"
type LINE 3000,-2200 3000,5800 ;
type TRIM
pick 3000,-1300
pick 3000,5000
enter
wait 1.5
caption "Offset" "OFFSET makes parallel copies at a distance"
type OFFSET 400
pick 6000,2800
pick 6900,2800
pick 4200,2000
pick 3000,2000
enter
wait 2
zoom extents
caption "Next: levels and walls" "Tutorial 04 starts the Cedar House"
wait 3
